{"id": "haiku__GEN__omni_405__3", "result": "Let $a = 2001^{1002}$, so $a^{-1} = 2001^{-1002}$.\n\nThen $x = a - a^{-1}$ and $y = a + a^{-1}$.\n\nUsing the difference of squares:\n\n$$x^2 - y^2 = (x-y)(x+y)$$\n\nHere $x - y = -2a^{-1}$ and $x + y = 2a$, so\n\n$$x^2 - y^2 = (-2a^{-1})(2a) = -4.$$\n\nCheck by expanding: $x^2 = a^2 - 2 + a^{-2}$ and $y^2 = a^2 + 2 + a^{-2}$, so $x^2 - y^2 = -4$.\n\nANSWER: -4", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.00035989, "model_used": ["claude-haiku-5-5"], "secs": 3.7}